Upstream-PR: ci: build a linux-riscv64 prebuild and ship it in the release tarballs
Upstream-Repo: https://github.com/websockets/bufferutil
Upstream-Base: v4.2.0 (d8aa572)
Upstream-Files: .github/workflows/ci.yml

Why: bufferutil publishes prebuilds for six platforms and none for linux-riscv64, so every
riscv64 consumer compiles the addon on install. The addon is plain C with no
architecture assumptions, so one more prebuild row closes that gap.

What changes: a build-riscv64 job that runs upstream's own `npm run prebuild` on a
riscv64 runner - prebuildify names the output after the host architecture, so
emulation would not produce the expected directory - and one extra tar line in the
release job, so the artifact ships next to the other six.

How it was tested: this addon was built and tested on riscv64 (upstream's own mocha
suite, then the prebuild loaded with node_modules/build removed), and the resulting
file is a RISC-V ELF named prebuilds/linux-riscv64/bufferutil.node, which is exactly what
node-gyp-build resolves there.

Note: this patch is NOT applied by the composite action in this repository (see
.dsh/plan.md D34). It is kept here so the increment can be submitted upstream as is.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index a20bb8e..d7315e6 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -79,8 +79,29 @@ jobs:
           name: ${{ matrix.os }}-${{ matrix.arch }}
           path: prebuilds
           retention-days: 1
+  build-riscv64:
+    if: startsWith(github.ref, 'refs/tags/')
+    needs: test
+    # GitHub has no hosted riscv64 runner, and prebuildify names the directory after
+    # the host's own architecture, so this has to run on a real riscv64 machine
+    # rather than under emulation. Relabel the runner if yours is named differently.
+    runs-on: [self-hosted, linux, riscv64]
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v7
+      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7
+        with:
+          node-version: 22
+      - run: npm install
+      - run: npm run prebuild
+      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7
+        with:
+          name: ubuntu-22.04-riscv64
+          path: prebuilds
+          retention-days: 1
   release:
-    needs: build
+    needs:
+      - build
+      - build-riscv64
     permissions:
       contents: write # Needed for softprops/action-gh-release.
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
@@ -103,6 +124,9 @@ jobs:
       - run:
           tar -cvf "${{ steps.get_version.outputs.version }}-linux-arm64.tar"
           -C "prebuilds/ubuntu-24.04-arm-arm64" linux-arm64
+      - run:
+          tar -cvf "${{ steps.get_version.outputs.version }}-linux-riscv64.tar" -C
+          "prebuilds/ubuntu-22.04-riscv64" linux-riscv64
       - run:
           tar -cvf "${{ steps.get_version.outputs.version }}-win32-ia32.tar" -C
           "prebuilds/windows-latest-x86" win32-ia32
